; AX3042 carries a machine-applicable fix: the tag line, inserted at
; the start of the line that holds the declaration - `~>` with a
; zero-width span, which AXDL spells `L:C` with no end column.
;
; `greet` has a `::` signature on the line above its `fn`, and the
; fix still lands at the `fn` line: a tag attaches to the NEXT
; declaration after it, so between the signature and the `fn` is
; where this language writes one. Applied by hand while this case was
; written, the result checks clean.
;
; The prose is now two helps: the one that carries the fix says only
; what to write, because an editor shows a fix's help as the action's
; title; the transitivity paragraph follows as a second help.
;
; `main` draws it too, since 2026-08-29, and did not before: `(println
; who)` renders `who` through `show`, whose four implementations made
; `greet`'s row carry one row-global over-approximation marker, and
; `main` inherited the marker with the IO and was excused on it.
; Over-approximation is per effect now, and the IO here is definite
; (tests/diagnostics/381-effect-through-callee.ax is the full shape).
(import IO)

(:: greet (-> String Int))
(fn (greet who)
  {
    (println who)
    0
  })

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (greet "hi"))
